ty density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{5}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}+\\frac{1}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{45}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427361 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427349 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427361 1069 "q-152894" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427361 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427361 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}},\\,x\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427361 1072 #uuid "2ced0c63-cf37-5cdb-ae0d-645ad331eb6b" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427361 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{{x}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{\\infty }{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{1}^{a}{x}^{-3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-2{x}^{-1/2})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}})|}_{1}^{a} \\\\  & =-5{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{a}}-1) \\\\  & =-5(0-1) \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427362 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427358 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427362 1069 "q-152916" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427362 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427362 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,1\\le x\\le 2.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{5}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427362 1072 #uuid "2dabf35b-e60b-5d7b-a653-f44f57203be2" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427362 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fifth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(16-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427363 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427353 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427363 1069 "q-152918" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427363 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427363 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 2.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{5}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427363 1072 #uuid "4c7b6764-ca2b-56e1-8efb-c299f7c5895e" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427363 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fifth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(64-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{16}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427364 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427348 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427364 1069 "q-131141" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427364 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427364 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{2x},\\,{e}^{-2}<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}},$ compute $\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427364 1072 #uuid "63bcffd8-dbf0-5c48-8ca6-56531c05d1c3" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427364 1074 "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X]=4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{{e}^{-2}}^{1}\\frac{x}{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}\\,|}_{{e}^{-2}}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[4{X}^{2}-2X] & =4\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-2\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =4(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{4{e}^{4}})-2(\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2{e}^{2}}) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}-1+\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{e}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{{e}^{4}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427365 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427347 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427365 1069 "q-152921" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427365 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427365 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{x}^{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}, & 1<x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{5}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427365 1072 #uuid "6e408aa1-cabb-5d40-b79a-58877a0c50b9" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427365 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fifth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{5}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{5}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\cdot (1-{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{5}-{x}^{8})\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}\\,{x}^{6}-\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{9}){|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{24}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{9}-0)+\\frac{1}{24}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{21}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{193}{72}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427366 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427352 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427366 1069 "q-152923" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427366 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427366 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{4}, & 0\\le x<1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\,x, & 1\\le x\\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{4}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427366 1072 #uuid "6e9a565a-12f8-5f6b-b609-40f05cb5f2ab" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427366 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the fourth raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{4}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{4}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{12}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{12}(64-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{20}+\\frac{21}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{53}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427367 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427357 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427367 1069 "q-90451" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427367 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427367 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}+1].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=1-\\frac{x}{4},\\,1<x<3\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427367 1072 #uuid "78882664-5ca1-5d0e-9798-9cca3f283762" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427367 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}+1]=2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+1\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot (1-\\frac{x}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{3}({x}^{2}-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{16}){|}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{11}{3}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}+1] & =2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+1 \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{11}{3}+1 \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427368 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427346 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427368 1069 "q-152899" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427368 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427368 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & -1<x<0, \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\,x, & 0\\le x<1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427368 1072 #uuid "84598522-637e-5d77-b555-f1f4d414ed22" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427368 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{2}\\cdot {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3}\\,x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{x}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{4}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\,{x}^{5}\\,{|}_{-1}^{0}+\\frac{1}{3}\\,{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}(0+1)+\\frac{1}{3}(1-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427369 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427355 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427369 1069 "q-90454" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427369 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427369 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=4{x}^{3},\\,0<x<1\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{4}{5},$ compute $\\text{E}[9{X}^{2}+X].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427369 1072 #uuid "8ee689ae-d309-5b9e-a1ff-6e4de3b135ae" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427369 1074 "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[9{X}^{2}+X]=9\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+\\text{E}[X]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot 4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\,|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{4}{5}$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=\\frac{2}{3}$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[9{X}^{2}+X] & =9\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]+\\text{E}[X] \\\\  & =9\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =6+\\frac{4}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{34}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427370 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427354 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427370 1069 "q-131143" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427370 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427370 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5].$\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,0<x<3\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427370 1072 #uuid "90065876-8b39-51cd-875c-5aa5721dc0eb" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427370 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5]=2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=3$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2{X}^{2}-5] & =2\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-5 \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427371 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427350 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427371 1069 "q-131152" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427371 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427371 1071 "The continuous random variable $X$ has the following probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\,1<x<2\n$$\n\nGiven that $\\text{E}[X]=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,$ compute $\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}].$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that $\\text{E}[aX+bY]=a\\text{E}[X]+b\\text{E}[Y]$ for any random variables $X$ and $Y$ and constants $a$ and $b.$*" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427371 1072 #uuid "993709fe-5242-5062-93c5-df6c430c3cdf" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427371 1074 "First, we simplify using the hint and the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}]=2\\text{E}[X]-5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the $n$th raw moment of $X$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{n}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{n}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe already know $\\text{E}[X].$ So, we compute the second raw moment of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}2\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2x\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\text{E}[X]=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ and $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]=2$ into the simplified expression, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[2X-5{X}^{2}] & =2\\text{E}[X]-5\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] \\\\  & =2\\cdot 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427372 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427351 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427372 1069 "q-152900" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427372 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427372 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}, & 0<x<1, \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}, & 1\\le x<2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427372 1072 #uuid "9e993c85-9e06-5795-8658-efd529bfafbc" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427372 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, we compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{8}{3}\\,{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}\\,{x}^{6}\\,{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{1}{9}\\,{x}^{3}\\,{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}(1-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(8-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{11}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427373 1068 #edb/ref 17592186427359 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427373 1069 "q-152893" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427373 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427373 1071 "A continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,1\\le x\\le e.\n$$\n\nCalculate $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427373 1072 #uuid "da4e5265-9949-5f02-b346-af79bf8d00ab" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true] [17592186427373 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]={\\int }_{S}{x}^{2}\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nWe compute the expected value of ${X}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{e}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2}-1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534599 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-00ec450b-8c39-502c-a433-fd5a4ae4c4b0" 17592186427276 "answer-044244e8-f2a2-5ef1-8833-22499068eac4" 17592186427277 "answer-09fdd550-bf28-5f33-af90-7628e13259a1" 17592186427278 "answer-0addfc1b-9d02-54e5-8a6c-dd9cd58986f2" 17592186427279 "answer-0b9101a2-c4eb-5ffc-8017-56ef5d0f4631" 17592186427280 "answer-1787c976-b394-5db2-9647-7788ad9018da" 17592186427281 "answer-17b6397b-6d8a-502f-b1bb-d6805bac1e89" 17592186427282 "answer-17fc818e-1be8-57fa-8910-2ceb34d1bfea" 17592186427283 "answer-18dde701-e4cf-5985-910b-d99d3686a2e6" 17592186427284 "answer-1b9fa685-0872-591b-81b4-ec8fbd0394aa" 17592186427285 "answer-1e10a00b-59c4-5c6b-a991-01b8fe10266b" 17592186427286 "answer-208a0b10-d20c-5680-b78b-191ae08c910b" 17592186427287 "answer-216706e8-4838-5204-973c-827cb86e9697" 17592186427288 "answer-2eb44b98-48db-57a3-ba4e-4af609be3544" 17592186427289 "answer-2fa99956-5688-5c52-8334-d71d3728db7c" 17592186427290 "answer-33cb4776-7d73-5e89-be66-3abb80c22cd1" 17592186427291 "answer-3b15167c-cc7e-5c97-9101-4beaf41df4c2" 17592186427292 "answer-473710fd-9ead-5a45-b8c2-95659c60b704" 17592186427293 "answer-4965166b-8ac3-5114-9933-f4b87cef16a0" 17592186427294 "answer-4a13ee3f-d613-5356-b098-bfd4fd31aaad" 17592186427295 "answer-4c69f0cd-2d3b-5d9b-93f3-eb5246d17118" 17592186427296 "answer-524c0c3b-a863-56ca-980e-5d3036687f18" 17592186427297 "answer-561a582b-3336-5381-80c8-bea3d50931a1" 17592186427298 "answer-5871acd5-eca9-59af-9564-3f4745f98b8e" 17592186427299 "answer-5b4af875-f9cd-5e54-964a-6b3e0fd19b65" 17592186427300 "answer-5d5bf664-a18f-566d-a4f7-3bd738b55f2b" 17592186427301 "answer-6292f7a0-9113-56c4-bf5e-7d9